  "term": "mesencephalon",
  "definition": "The mesencephalon is the embryonic middle brain vesicle that becomes the midbrain. In the mature brain, it is a short region linking the pons and diencephalon and includes dorsal and ventral parts involved in visual, auditory, and other sensorimotor functions.",
